# Force LF for shebang-bearing script files. On Windows checkouts with
# core.autocrlf=true, these were silently converted to CRLF, which corrupts
# the shebang line for tools that expect a bare "\n" after "#!...". In
# particular, Vite/Vitest's SSR import transform (getFileStartIndex, driven
# by the regex /^#!.*\n/ in vite/dist/node/chunks/node.js) fails to detect a
# CRLF-terminated shebang, falls back to hoisting rewritten imports at
# position 0, and ends up inserting code BEFORE the shebang line -- producing
# "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token" when such a file is imported by
# a Vitest test (see scripts/check-route-guards.mjs +
# __tests__/unit/api/route-guards.test.ts).
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.sh  text eol=lf
